    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        40,
        1520
      ],
      "size": [
        930,
        700
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 18,
      "mode": 0,
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "IMAGE + RECORDED SPEECH -> WAN v9 -> RIFE -> LatentSync 1.6 -> SPAN -> Mosaic -> MP4\nUpload one image and one 0.5–6s dialogue file, edit motion prompt, then Run once. No text-to-speech or LTX model.\nSpeech Plan checks a single detectable face BEFORE WAN sampling and sets WAN frame count automatically.\nKeep face visible, near frontal, not tiny or covered. Anime detection/visual quality requires a real test.\nThis is NOT a seamless loop: speech drives mouth timing. No inserted first image, reverse/ping-pong, speech truncation or speed change.\nOutput: 25 FPS (LatentSync native), speech duration rounded UP by <40ms, silence only at the very end. Original voice, AAC.\nRIFE resamples source motion before mouth sync. Do NOT interpolate/trim after sync. SPAN does not change timing.\nWAN checkpoints/sampler/optional LoRAs unchanged. LatentSync uses 20 steps / guidance1.5 / 512 face crop; it unloads WAN GPU models first.\nNo DeepCache. Higher guidance can distort faces; more steps cost time. No claim of GPU validation or unchanged face quality.\nLip-sync runtime/models: special lip-sync image, LIPSYNC_PROFILE=latentsync-1.6, AUDIO_PROFILE=none. +5.50 GB weights.\nFace weights (InsightFace buffalo_l) are restricted to non-commercial research. Check all model licenses before use.\nMosaic is output-only, after lip sync and SPAN. Always inspect final frames; automated detection is not guaranteed."
      ],
      "title": "READ ME · Quality / speed / loop boundaries"
    },
